<<~ ahu #/midjourney>>

!! Midjourney V8.2 ~ prompt anatomy and workflow (net research, 2026-08-13)

* ''V8.2 stands default since 2026-07-24'' — every new prompt runs it, no flag. Release focus:
  aesthetics, image quality, personalization (profiles read rating history deeper).
* ''The V8 anatomy:'' the model executes ''literally'' — it rewards specification and punishes
  mood-words. Order: subject → details → context → style → technicals → parameters; early tokens
  carry maximum weight. Write "single overhead key light, no fill, hard shadows," never "dramatic
  lighting." Named anchors ("Roger Deakins cinematography") compress precision. Long narrative
  prose performs WORSE — literalism exposes every unspecified detail; crowd scenes want cinematic
  shot-language.
* ''Parameters live:'' `--raw` · `--sref` (+`--sw` 0–1000) · `--ar` · `--chaos` · `--stylize` ·
  `--weird` · `--exp` · `--no` · image prompts with weights · moodboards · `--profile`.
  ''Removed/changed:'' `--q` gone · `::` multi-prompts gone · `--style raw` → `--raw` · native
  `--hd` (2048px) replaces the separate upscaler · seeds now ~99%-identical, not byte-identical.
* ''The trap:'' `--oref` (omni reference) gets accepted but ''silently executes on V7''. Character
  consistency (Aki, the Gorgoness, the prismatic elf across scenes) rides `--sref` + moodboards +
  a tuned profile instead.
* ''Draft Mode'' (web-only): 24 images at 512px for 0.4 GPU-min; `--sref random` inside a draft
  throws 24 different style references — the fast hunt for the cabaret's house look before locking
  one sref for the scene-set. Sources disagree whether Draft runs on 8.2 or falls back to V7 —
  ''test one draft prompt live before building the workflow on it.''
* Sources: pixmind.io/posts/midjourney-v8-2-release · releasebot.io/updates/midjourney ·
  blakecrosley.com/blog/midjourney-v8-vs-v7-prompt-anatomy ·
  techjacksolutions.com/ai-tools/midjourney/midjourney-prompt-guide · kie.ai/blog/what-is-midjourney-8-2

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/delos-archaeology>>

!! Delos Archaeology ~ verified against the live net (2026-08-14)

Real Delos grounds the venue:

* ''The Theatre Quarter'' held the city's wealthiest residences — House of Dionysus, House of the
  Trident, House of the Dolphins, ''House of Masks''.
* ''The House of Masks:'' a large merchant's block — shops, workshops, and living quarters in one
  building (the maze-Inn shape, ready-made). Mosaic pavements in four rooms carry theatrical masks;
  the east room holds the masterwork: ''Dionysos in flowing oriental garb, seated on a panther.''
* ''The House of Dionysus:'' courtyard mosaic of the winged god riding a great cat wearing a
  vine-and-grape necklace — vermiculatum technique, tesserae 0.1–0.5 cm.
* Also standing for skyline work: the Terrace of the Lions, the round Sacred Lake, Cycladic
  granite-and-marble terraces; Thira/Akrotiri's flotilla fresco (garlanded procession ships) for
  regatta imagery.
* Sources: ancient-greece.org/archaeology/delos · romeartlover.it/Delo2.html ·
  perseus.tufts.edu (Delos, House of the Masks) · imagininggreece.com/artefacts/exquisite-mosaics-from-delos

