<<~ ahu #/negentropy>>

!! Negentropy ~ the canon gaps (five settled 2026-08-15, two open)

Mythology-sourced proposals — ''each fixes first canon only on the operator's word''. Items 1–5
stand BLESSED (2026-08-15) and seated: the venue in `high-delos-cabaret.mem`, the Lindwyrm body
in the referee dossier, the Gorgonne canon in `factions/gorgonne-diaspora.mem`, the Amaranth
livery in `factions/order-of-amaranth.mem`, the court colors in `factions/index.mem`. Items 6–7
(the skyline dressing, the trireme's face) ride open still:

# ''The venue — SETTLED: The House of Masks.'' Canon seats in `high-delos-cabaret.mem` #venue:
  the Inn stands as the levitated House of Masks of old Delos's Theatre Quarter, the cabaret floor
  keeping the Dionysos-on-panther mosaic the speakeasy hid under boards. The six proposals below
  ride Provisional still.
# ''The Lindwyrm's body'' (BLESSED; register per Freyja 2026-08-15). Heraldic lindworm law:
  ''wingless, serpentine, two forelimbs'' — Master-tier heritage with ''levitation-flight'': she
  flies the way rivers swim. ''Render register:'' very eastern — ''Miyazaki / Earthsea /
  Spirited-Away'' dragon-language (the river-spirit line) crossed with the ''German wingless''
  lindworm — never the winged Western wyrm. Folktale seam (Prince Lindworm / King Lindorm):
  transformation by ''shedding skins'' — her humanoid dragon-kin form reads as a kept shed skin
  worn like couture; the mana-muting glamour as "the last shift." Scales in orichalcum-sheen.
# ''The Gorgoness + crew.'' Archaic Gorgons carried wings and bronze hands; the Hellenistic
  "beautiful Medusa" type gives the captain's face. Crew as ''Euryale-line'' ("the far-roaming" —
  a sailor's lineage): serpent braids dressed with coin-rings, small bronze wing-vestiges at the
  temples, ''smoked-glass gaze-spectacles'' (welds to the Ray-Bane Navigators status-spectacle
  canon — gorgonne courtesy invented the fashion). Shipboard mirror-taboos.
# ''Order of Amaranth livery.'' Amaranth crimson-magenta over unbleached linen and bone-white;
  dried amaranth chaplets at the shoulder, unfading while iron rusts; tarnished-silver flower pins.
  Sacrament from Gaia's ritual record (Aztec huautli / alegría): ''amaranth-grain honey bread''
  broken for guest-right — sanctuary law made edible.
# ''Court color regimes'' (derived from the ch05 court-dragon table, never invented whole):
  Seelie gold + summer green · Unseelie black + winter violet · Ouroborous blue + bronze
  serpent-scale · Brimstone sulfur-yellow + ember red + ash grey.
# ''High Delos skyline'' //(researched 2026-08-15, net-verified; ''the Colossus weld BLESSED
  2026-08-15'' — civic-scale ley-line node, Temple-tier Lares, seated in the region worksheet;
  the rest of the dressing rides Provisional)//: ''Mount Kynthos'' (113m, the pre-Greek summit precinct — cave shrines and temples
  to foreign gods) crowns the sky-island; the ''Terrace of the Lions'' (Naxian archaic marble,
  ~600 BC, originally nine-to-sixteen, stylized and formal) lines its processional road gazing
  over open cloud where the Sacred Lake's water used to answer them; the round ''Sacred Lake''
  hangs as a pool on the island's underside; and the ''Naxian Colossus'' — the nine-meter archaic
  Apollo — stands proposed as THE great Lares statue of Elyncia_02 canon ("orichalcum runes…
  stone eyes flared with inner light"): the colossus rode the levitation and serves now as a
  Temple-tier node. Cycladic granite terraces; theatre-quarter mosaics; regatta weather outside
  the cabaret windows.
# ''The flying trireme's face'' //(researched 2026-08-15, net-verified; rides Provisional until
  blessed)//: real triremes wore ''marble ophthalmoi'' — appliqué eyes, six preserved from the
  Zea ship-sheds, irises rendered in paint, left and right eyes distinct, ''the lacrimal duct
  carved at the inner corner''. Proposal: the eyes ride as Named wards, and the carved tear-duct
  runs functional — ''a Named ship can weep, and captains read the tears''. The ram follows the
  Athlit law: ''one single bronze casting'' (the surviving original: 465 kg, cast whole) — a
  Named ram must be one pour. The lower two oar-banks fuse into fixed ''mana-foil vanes''
  shimmering like oars frozen mid-stroke; the top bank still rows — ceremony, and captains who
  distrust a ship that cannot feel its water. Festival dress per the Akrotiri flotilla frieze:
  flower garlands, butterfly-and-swallow pennants, canopied ikria shading the passengers, the
  procession running town to town — and dolphins, which at altitude becomes a question the
  renders get to answer.

Folklore legs still riding unverified weights (collide before canon-doc use): the Prince-Lindworm
skin-count, the archaic-Gorgon bronze-hands attribution, the huautli compression.

