<<~ ahu #/witness-heritage>>

!! Spirit Witness ~ the Fae Casting Bench (FTLS ch03)

Glimmer-Count's hand-back, ''verbatim'' — the full heritage inventory: 34 fae heritages, the four flagged casts (changeling · dragon-kin · gorgonne · prismatic elf), and the cabaret bench in three tiers.

```text
**Active Voice: Lares (Tasked Spirit)** — no fuller Voice-house roster reached me in this task packet; I stood the scout under the Lares seed only. Flagging that as a gap rather than inventing names.

---

## 1. READ COMPLETENESS

| File | Status |
|---|---|
| `/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/ftls/Flying_Triremes_and_Laser_Swords_03_OSR_Heritage_Trait.md` | **COMPLETE** — all 1,629 lines read (catalogue L89–342, heritages L344–1629) |
| `/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/ftls/Flying_Triremes_and_Laser_Swords_04_Recon_Salvage_Secrets.md` | **STUB read** — headings + keyword grep only. **VERDICT: effectively zero heritage/fae content.** Only 3 incidental hits: L429 "Brimstone Fae Mining Kit" (toolkit name), L694 "Fairy's Death (OGA)" `[illegal][glass][anti-fae][concealed]` knife, L14 company framing. Chapter is RSS logistics/salvage/recipes. Not usable for casting. |
| Other ftls chapters | grep-only, line refs below |

---

## 2. MECHANICAL SHAPE (applies to every heritage)

`03:8–26` — Heritage is **free at creation, occupies no Trait slot**. Ranks: **Skilled = 3 effects / +3 heritage lore; Expert = 4 / +6; Master = 5 / +9** (`03:10–14`, `03:81`). Effects drawn from the Heritage Effect Catalogue. "Mark your Heritage" is the activation currency; unmark by 1 watch rest, 10 min + 1 Life, or 1 action + 1 Ability damage (`03:26`).

**Setting rule that makes ALL of this fae — quote, `03:1014`:**
> "In the Vastlands, all folk are human at heart; in Elyncia, *all human folk are faerie‑folk*."

And `03:85`: *"Heritages are not factions... Everyone has someone in their family or community who expresses the faerie magic differently."*

---

## 3. SPECIFICALLY FLAGGED (parent's four asks)

### CHANGELING (PC) — `03:1028`
**Not a standalone heritage. A Human VARIANT.**
Base **Human** (`03:1005–1030`): Skilled = Jack of All Trades + Bonus Background (counts as a Heritage effect, not a Trait slot) + Choose one. Expert = Lucky. Master = Affinity – Hearth & Ways.
> **Changeling:** "Humans born closer to the Fae Courts, they weave illusion and dream‑logic with ease. Skilled: Choose **Affinity – Illusion • Light • Void** or **Affinity – Chaos • Dream • Shadow**." (`03:1028`)

Visual: no dedicated changeling appearance line. Human appearance is `03:1020`: *"Infinite variation, from market‑hardened wanderers to velvet‑court diplomats."* Culture line worth mining for a youth PC — `03:1023`: *"families that host **pixie fosterlings**"* — the fosterling motif is the textual hook for a changeling-human youth.
Ch10 Human hooks (`10:568–577`) include `10:571` a Human diplomat making PCs pose as her "fae retainers" at a **voidjammer banquet** — near-exact cabaret-adjacent seed.

### DRACONIC / DRAGON-KIN (Lindwyrm arrival) — `03:619–648`
**Dragonborn.** Skilled: Affinity (choose tag-set) + Armoured Body + one (common: Spirited / Fly / Climb / Inner Fire). Expert: **Chimeric Body**. Master: Affinity – Serpent Energy.
> `03:640` — **"The Dragonborn clans practice the Draconic lineage of Chimeric Body, shifting from draconic humanoids to six limbed mythic beasts."** ← this is the exact mechanic for "arrives as humanoid dragon-kin." Common chimeric effects: Aggressive, Fly/Hover, Solid, Size–Large.

Visual, `03:632`: *"scales of chroma-sheen or hammered metal; ember eyes; some bear wing-stubs, some spined crests."*
Culture, `03:628–635`: honor codes and hoard-rites "older than the Bronze Sky"; *"debate beneath obsidian arches, measure worth in gifts of metals and glass"*; hoards as community banks (take one gem, repay two); taboo: break no contracted word. Names: Klauthrax, Aurix-Vara, Nalkyria, Vezzen-Steel, Jivali-Ember.
**Four sub-lineages** (`03:641–648`): **Chromatic** (Red/Blue/Green/Black/White — mercurial raiders, lightning duels, sky-games, breath weapons, usually take Fly); **Metallic** (Gold/Silver/Bronze/Copper — philosophic wardens, hoards of treaties, Hover); **Gem** (Amethyst/Emerald/Sapphire/Onyx — *"Psychic crystal-singers and void duelists; luminous mirrors of thought & light"*, Illusion•Light•Void); **Dream** (Dream/Octarine/Noosphere/Shadow — *"Rare cosmic brood; speak in stellar equations and lost riddles, practices shadow-fire magics"*).

Lindwyrm-specific canon lives **outside** ch03 — `01:179`: *"The Lindwyrm, Patron of New Delos"* is classed as an **embodied immortal / demi-god / durable avatar-being**, "closer to this category than to the vast distributed condition of most gods," and such beings "may rule cities, command fleets, bargain face-to-face, or appear repeatedly in the same body." **This is the only Lindwyrm text in the ftls corpus.**
Also `05:837` **Faerie Court ↔ Dragon alignment table** (Rod of the Wyrm): **Seelie/Gold**, **Ouroborous/Blue**, **Unseelie/Black** — a canonical three-Court dragon taxonomy usable for Lindwyrm court-alignment color at a Delos scene.

### GORGON / MEDUSA-KIN (Gorgoness captain + crew) — `03:1286`
**Not standalone. A Plane Touched theme: "🐍 Gorgonne."**
Base **Plane Touched** (`03:1250–1288`): Skilled = Lucky + choose two from {Spirited, Affinity, Aggressive ("hair‑serpents snap, halo‑wings buffet, strange limbs lash"), Alternate Movement, Armoured Body ("bone‑plates, shard‑halos, void‑aura"), Chimeric Body, Darkvision, Polybody ("you are a swarm"), Psi‑Speech, Size}. Expert = one more/upgrade. Master = **Paradox Die** (mark Heritage, add d6 to any roll, then Danger Roll vs the final Paradox modifier — reality glitches).
> **Gorgonne, `03:1286`:** "Skilled: Choose **Affinity – Serpent Energy**; your **hair‑serpents are spirit‑familiars** and your clan teaches the ***Serpent's Gaze*** power (heritage power, **50% discount**) which you can overcharge for strange effects. Choose one other effect. Expert: the spirit-serpent folk often choose **Chimeric Form** or **Inspiration** and collect other secret powers."

Critical casting note — the base Plane Touched appearance line **already names a gorgon captain**, `03:1273`:
> "Varies wildly: statuesque beings with radiant cracks, drifting silhouettes with masks for faces, **captains with serpents for braids**, and void‑fragments stitched into cloaks."

Plus `03:1269`: *"They might wear serpent‑spirits in their hair, wear masks that whisper truths in moonlight, or leak halos of unsteady light. When they speak, glass might frost or flowers might bloom in desert sand."* Names: Whispercoil, Foxfire-on-the-Sea, Vox Tenebris, Glass-Wing, Umbral-Dawn, Parallax. Culture (`03:1277`): *"Found wherever the unreal bleeds into the real: on **skyjammer decks**, in labyrinthine Courts, beneath starlit bridges."*
Ch10 hooks: `10:651` *"The Snake in Her Hair — One of a Gorgonne's serpent‑spirits went rogue and now whispers treason into strangers' dreams."* `10:653` *"Impossible Port — A captain's skyjammer moors at a harbor that doesn't exist; the PCs are invited aboard."*
**Note:** ch06 gorgon hits (`06:7153, 7168, 7212, 7227, 8852`) are all **petrification-breath monster rules**, not heritage — do not use for the Gorgoness captain.

### PRISMATIC / CHROMATIC ELF (PC) — two candidate sources, they are DIFFERENT things

**(a) Spectrum Satrap** — `03:1449–1474`. The literal prismatic heritage.
Skilled: Armoured Body ×1 + choose two (common: Spirited / **Affinity – Illusion•Light•Void** / Psi‑Speech).
Expert: **Blinding Brilliance** — mark Heritage, flare with impossible light (20 yd); all Save vs Aura; hostiles who fail blinded 1d6 rounds (roll once for all); allies who succeed get Advantage on next roll.
Master: **Prismatic Ascension** — mark Heritage, become a coherent lightform for one watch (4h): fly at double Speed, slip through keyhole-wide gaps, +9 Defense (mundane attacks pass through), Life worth double power for [illusion]/[light]/[void] powers.
> Description `03:1461`: "Prismatic 'para‑humans' from the **Violet Steppe and the Black City's shimmering palaces**... **Bright-colored suits cover their bodies, glass helmets conceal their heads.** Their bodies refract and glow, shifting through hues like diplomatic flags. They are emissaries, tyrants, and mystics all at once — and when they decide to become pure light, entire rooms obey."
> Appearance `03:1465`: "Skin and carapace shimmer from **mother‑of‑pearl to oil‑slick black**; **eyes like cut gems**."
> Culture `03:1468`: "**Prism‑banquets where wine is color‑coded for emotion**; courts that outlaw 'dull' colors; **holy duels of projected light‑forms**." ← strongest single cabaret-scene line in the whole chapter.
Names: Lazul, Corind, Opalin, Saphra, Prisme, Aurion.
Variants: **Chroma Courtier** (*"diplomats whose mirror-helms shimmer with etiquette glyphs; they duel with cutting compliments and projected light-forms, tuning their hues to sway crowds and unnerve rivals"* — swap Armoured×2 for Armoured + Spirited); **Umbral Satrap** (*"Eclipse-born shadow envoys who trade in forgotten memories, and command shadows to stitch corridors between sleeping courts"* — swap Illusion•Light•Void for Chaos•Dream•Shadow).

**(b) Elf** — `03:684–706`. Not described as prismatic, but Illusion includes prismatic glamour.
Skilled: Quick + Darkvision + Lucky. Expert: **Affinity – Illusion • Light • Void**. Master: Psi‑Speech.
Relevant: `03:127` Affinity Illusion•Light•Void text — *"Weave fae-charms and reality edits, bend radiance and reflection, or veil yourself in void-glamours. **Illusion includes prismatic glamour** and the push-pull of reality/unreality."* ← this is the rules text that licenses an Elf PC reading as "prismatic."
> Description `03:692`: "The **Elf** clans are paradoxes draped in velvet—envoys of unthinkable Courts, darlings of decadence, and half‑willing hosts to the echoes of distant stars. They walk Elyncia's halls and void‑bridges with a **glamour that is both invitation and warning**. To mortals, they are dazzling; to older beings, they are dutiful children of cruel patrons."
> Appearance `03:696`: "**Angular beauty, void‑shadowed eyes, hair like moonlit ink or starlit fire.**"
> Culture `03:699`: "**Moon‑wine feasts under mirrored sky‑domes**, ritual duels fought as much with etiquette as with blades, **salons where voidjammer pilots trade stories with dream‑witches**." ← second-strongest cabaret line.
Voice `03:698`: *"voices like honey poured through crystal"*; debts measured in centuries.
Variants: Void Envoy (Master: swap Psi‑Speech → Armoured Body); **Glass‑Mask Courtier** (*"Endlessly adaptable, trained in mortal manners and void‑court graces alike"*; Master: Psi‑Speech → Jack of All Trades); **Shadow Elves** (*"More comfortable in the shadows and dream-realms than the bright light of the crystal ballrooms"*; Expert: Illusion•Light•Void → Chaos•Dream•Shadow).

**Recommendation for the parent:** a "prismatic elf PC" is best built as **Elf + Affinity Illusion•Light•Void** (per `03:127`), with **Spectrum Satrap** reserved for a separate NPC caste — the Satraps are helmeted/suited para-humans, not elves.

---

## 4. CABARET-STAFF / PERFORMER CANDIDATES (winged, glowing, shapeshifting, musical)

Ranked by fit, all from ch03.

**TIER 1 — built for this scene**

- **Faun Folk** `03:714–735` — *hook line in the ToC (`03:46`) is literally "Festival guides & hosts."* Skilled: Fortunate (+1 CHA, +1 Ward) + Quick + Nimble. Expert: Affinity – Hearth & Ways. Master: **Inspiration** (aura: allies within (Level+CHA)×10 yd get +1 all action rolls and +1 Morale). Description `03:722`: *"Hoof-light children of vine and song... live for the pulse of festival drums... Their laughter carries the scent of wild honey; their **horns curl like question marks that dare mortals to dance**."* Appearance `03:726`: *"Lean bodies, goat or deer legs, small curling horns, **freckles like dappled sunlight**; garlands of ivy, bells, or **cork-wood pipes**."* Culture: wine rites "where promises ferment," masquerade hunts, **taboo on leaving a guest un-toasted**. Backgrounds: Vineyard Skald (Envoy), Wandering Bard (Sorcery). Variants: Forest Piper (Pan-follower, Masks & Totems), Mountain Satyr.
- **Spectrum Satrap** — see §3(b) above. Prism-banquets, color-coded wine, projected light-form duels. Perfect for the marquee act.
- **Elf** — see §3(b). Salons, moon-wine, mirrored sky-domes. Perfect for hosts/patrons.
- **Cat Lord** `03:555–576` — ToC hook `03:41`: *"**Velvet salon tyrants**."* Skilled: Quick + Size–Small + Psi‑Speech. Expert: Lucky. Master: Affinity – Serpent Energy. Description `03:563`: *"sinuous aristocrats of the strange — felines with weird traits like **living serpents as tails** who **rule tea‑houses and voidjammer lounges** with the same languid grace they stalk alleyways... whispers say they are the priests of the Purple God(dess), or the velvet‑pawed enforcers of some deeper Court."* Appearance `03:567`: *"Mythic cats with **jewel‑bright eyes**, prehensile paws, and sometimes a **serpent as a tail coiled like jewelry**."* Culture `03:570`: *"**Sunlit salons where deals are made over saucers of narcotic coffee**; charm‑sigils woven into rugs; **taboos against ignoring a Cat Lord's invitation (or worse — refusing it)**."* Voice: *"purrs that turn into commands."* Names: Brighteyes, Sleekums, Mazzo, Lady Elegant, Twinklestar, Mew‑Mew. **This is your house management / patron-tyrant tier.**
- **Quarterling – Pixie** `03:1349` — **winged staff.** *"Winged agents of chaos and wonder—equal parts living prank, and trickster‑courtier. **Wings from dragonfly‑glass to neon‑etched gossamer; clothes stitched from leaves, circuitry, or salvaged glamour.** Some flit between tree branches and teacups; **others ride data‑streams and voidjammer wake‑tides.**"* Skilled: swap Armoured Body → **Alternate Movement – Fly**. Expert: swap Inspiration → Illusion•Light•Void. Base Quarterling `03:1326–1341`: Armoured Body + Lucky + Size–Small; Expert Inspiration; Master Chaos•Dream•Shadow. Appearance `03:1338`: *"Small (3–4 ft) humanoids: fox‑ears, mossy tufts, soot‑smudged faces, blood‑streaked caps, greasy toolbelts, or **faint inner glow**."* Voice `03:1340`: *"Yapping, howling, shrill; even a whisper sounds like 'OI!'"* — good for barbacks/runners, not headliners. Other variants: Brownie, Spriggan/Boggart, Kobold, Red Cap, Gremlin/Imp (**Jinx** power, `03:1357`), **Gnome** (*"Curious void‑touched tinkers, **glowing from within**"*, Fly or Inner Fire).

**TIER 2 — glow / wing / shapeshift material**

- **Glow Kin (Fungi Folk)** `03:831–852` — bioluminescent, ToC hook *"Sporelight diplomats."* Appearance `03:843`: *"**Soft glow along gills and freckles; cap-crowns like mantles; filament 'hair'; spore halos in cold air; earthy perfumes that shift with mood.**"* Skilled: Spirited + Affinity Fungus&Spore + Psi‑Speech. Master: Chaos•Dream•Shadow. Culture: **fermentation banquets**, spore-communion rites. Psi‑Speech "carries taste/scent metaphors" — excellent for a non-verbal performer. Slime Kin variant: Amorphous Body, *"can choose to wear clothing, or seep through keyholes, **who split to multitask** and rejoin."*
- **Chimeric Folk (Centaur, Mythic, Shifter)** `03:584–611` — the shapeshifter/aerialist bench. Skilled: Affinity + **Chimeric Body** + one. Expert: **Chimeric Legacy** (all chimeric forms gain +1 effect, Speed +6 yd, Advantage vs shove/knockdown). Appearance `03:598`: *"Human-passing silhouettes with **evident tells: antlers, feathering along forearms, glossy chitin, leonine manes, lashing tails.**"* Voices *"carry drum-cadence, birdsong, or mask-speech."* **Mythic Families** `03:609`: **Harpy/Vulture Folk (Gale-Singers)**, Kirin/Qilin (Dream-Walker), Shedu/Lamassu (Threshold-Keeper), **Manticore (Court-Predator)**, **Sphinx (Riddle-Bearer)**, Gryphon/Hippogriff (Sky-Keeper). Culture: **mask-dances**, barding rites. *"a harpy's wind-oaths, a fox-spirit's mask-dance—none are taught lightly."* — **Gale-Singer harpies are your winged chorus; Sphinx is your riddling MC.**
- **Bird Folk** `03:467–487` — **Fly at Skilled.** Appearance `03:479`: *"Plumage varies by clan: **sunset crimsons, storm-cloud greys, iridescent midnight blues.** Lean, hollow-boned frames; **bright, ringed eyes**."* Expert: Affinity – **Air • Song • Storm**. Master: Chimeric Body. *"voices whistle and click like distant gulls."* Backgrounds include Spirit‑Mask Bard (Sorcery). Aeries *"woven of cloud-silk."*
- **Bat Folk** `03:409–430` — **Fly + Small at Skilled**, nocturnal. Appearance `03:421`: *"Slender bodies, oversized ears, dusk-coloured fur, **eyes that catch stray gleams like polished stone**."* **Echo-Singer variant** (`03:430`): *"Mystics who weave voices into ritual. Expert: Swap Nimble for **Inspiration**."* Master: Air•Song•Storm. Wing-tattoos mark coming of age. **Best fit for a torch-singer / house band.**
- **Frog Folk** `03:771–794` — **mood-bioluminescence + layered harmonic voice.** Appearance `03:783`: *"Glossy-skinned humanoids ranging from **pale mint to deep obsidian green**. Their **eyes reflect moonlight like still ponds**. **Skin may pulse with bioluminescence during strong emotions or ritual states.**"* Voice `03:785`: *"guttural bass tones, shimmering whistles, and **harmonic vibrations used in layered conversation. Silence is a language, too.**"* — a Frog Folk chorus is mechanically and visually distinct. "reed-flute storytellers."
- **Undead (Post Mortal) – Mirth‑Touched Shade** `03:1625` — *"Your ever-changing guise hides the truth within."* Skilled: Spirited + Affinity Masks & Totems. Base appearance `03:1616`: *"**lantern-glow in the chest or eyes**, pallid skin with bone glints, funerary inks and warding knots, reliquary charms, and tidy repairwork where life once failed."* Voices *"dry-echoed, wind-through-hollow, or **lantern-soft**."* Culture: *"they trade **passage songs** for true names."* — glowing, shapeshifting, musical, all three.
- **Plane Touched – Meta‑Angel** `03:1287` — Skilled: Size (Large or Small) + Affinity Illusion•Light•Void; *"you carry radiance, celestial edicts, or the stillness of perfect symmetry."* Expert: Chimeric Body + **Fly** + **Inspiration** (standing aura). **Winged, glowing, aura-buffing — headliner-grade.**
- **Porcelain Prince** `03:1296–1318` — decadent, masked, multi-bodied. `03:1312`: *"Ceremonial maskings, body labs that grow new drones, **decadent soirées where five mouths dine in unison and one body might not leave intact.**"* Appearance `03:1308`: *"Multiple identical bodies in **porcelain masks and lacquered armor**; some **crack to show the pale, patchworked flesh beneath.**"* Expert gives drones *"the 'ceramic aegis' look — **visible cracks and kintsugi‑style repairs that make them eerily beautiful.**"* — **a Polybody chorus line is one performer in Lv+2 bodies. Mechanically exact for synchronized dancers.**
- **Serpent Folk** `03:1420–1441` — *"Jade, obsidian, or bronze scales; slit-pupil eyes; **forked tongues that flicker with blue flame**; some bear ornate hood-crests or **cyber-gold implants**."* Cobra Oracle variant: *"Hood patterns hypnotise; royal courts pay for their dream-testimony."* Culture: *"**night markets trade dream-venom vials**." Pairs with the Gorgoness crew.

**TIER 3 — background/patron color**

Troll `03:1552` (8–12 ft, *"skin from storm‑blue to moss‑grey, sometimes veined with **glowing pebbles**"*, blood-crystal magitech scars, faerie toll-keepers) · Goblin `03:898–905` (*"skin like tarnished copper or sea-glass; over-large ears and **glitter-ink tattoos that rewrite themselves when nobody looks**"*; **Crystal Court Goblin** `03:910` *"serve the Labyrinth's elusive fae lord, juggling glass spheres and rewriting hallways"* — jugglers) · Hobgoblin `03:984–991` (*"**march in riotous colours, turning drill into festival**"*, lacquer masks, banner dyes, **nightly drill-dances** — precision dance troupe / door security) · Halfling `03:956` (*"trooping dancers under the moon"*, lantern feasts in hollow hills) · Spider Folk `03:1494` (*"multi-limbed silhouettes, glossy carapace over humanoid torso, **human faces with ocular clusters shimmering like dew**"*; silk aerialists — Affinity Silk & Web `03:197` *"Spin lines, sheets, **glamours**, and snares from web-silk... **elegant pranks**"*) · Mer Folk `03:1136` (*"slick skin veined with **opal scales**; ripple-fringed ears; **coral-grown jewelry**; **eyes like moonlit surf**"*) · Rabbit Folk – **Cryptid Hare (Pooka)** `03:1388` (*"**Moon-outlined silhouettes glimpsed only in rain or neon backlighting**; they tip nonexistent hats, nudge fate with gentle asides, and leave you laughing at jokes no one else heard"* — Illusion•Light•Void) · Nerthurian **Dryad** `03:1182` (*"sapwood bodies carry sunlight and birdsong"*, Power from the Sun) · Awakened Vome `03:387` (*"shells range from **sleek photonic composites to insectile chitin lattices; their movements sync to an inaudible beat**"* — literally dance to an unheard rhythm) · Ant Folk `03:360` (*"mottled carapace colours and **glowing body paint**"*).

