## 3. WORLD-DRESS VOCABULARY

- **Master tech line** — `Elyncia_01:90`: "**Power-armor crafted from bronze** and other resources… warriors brandish **laser swords that shimmer with arcane energy**. Elyncia's cultures have just prototyped '**flying triremes**' and other magitech vehicles… that **defy gravity with mana-foils**. The **wave-jammers** have existed since before the recent cataclysm, their **mana-foils letting them skim above the waters**. The rediscovery of '**power cores**'… have allowed the factions to evolve these into **sky-jammers** and the very rare and dangerous **void-jammers**."
- **Magic/tech law** — `Elyncia_01:62`: "'**magitech/oldtech**' and '**fantascience/sorcery**'"; Clarke + Pratchett both postulates.
- **Orichalcum forms:** inscribed magitech statues at ley-nodes (`Elyncia_01:70`); orichalcum runes on a great Lares statue whose "**stone eyes flared with inner light**" (`Elyncia_02:70`); orichalcum-inlaid archway warm to the touch (`Elyncia_04:98`); orichalcum-alloyed bronze helm (`Powered_Symbiote:121`); "**sandstone shot through with orichalcum veins**" (`Elyncia_01:718`); "**1-Orichalcum Guild certificates**" (`Sidebar_Lindwyrm…:6`); "prismatic ID keys" (`Sidebar_Alpha:140`).
- **Curse of Iron / rust-blooms** — `Elyncia_01:88`: "un-Named, untended worked iron **rots within weeks wherever a bloom runs**. Iron did not leave the world; it became *precious*… **kept behind immune-charms, tended like a relative**." `:169` "tools flaked, **bridges wept rust**, automata seized mid-stride"; `:175` "a **spore-lichen that grazes on sky-iron**"; `:205` "iron-bound chests… **split and rusted within days**"; `:287` "**comet-iron reefs where wild rust-blight strains nest thickest**"; `:309` "**cedar-resin woods that ward off rust-blight spores** (the lining of every serious iron-chest)"; `:191` "**quarantine rites at the adit mouths, spore-lamps burning, stores lined with Verdant Coil cedar and salt, every ingot tallied and charm-chained**"; `:727` "tokens crafted from **steel-less glass, immune to the Curse of Iron**."
- **Named iron** — `Elyncia_01:183`: "the naming rites double as **immune-charms**: the oiling, the ash and salt, the **rust-psalms**, the **yearly bathing of a blade like a relative**"; `:187` Brimstone crucible steel and **Named Firearms** "come out clean."
- **Order of Amaranth** — `Elyncia_01:88` "convoys it under the **sign of the unfading flower**"; `:191` "**anointing cargo with amaranth-oil** and putting blooms down hard when a cache turns"; `:422` "elite shock troops and seekers of ancient ruins"; `:415` "**Amaranth churches** — old ruined cathedrals, far flung monasteries, and **pop-up tent-churches**… Sanctuary offered, **violence kapu**"; `:586` "the **Keepers of the Unfading Seed**"; `:590` "known for **field medicine, sanctuary law, and an unnerving ease around the free-willed dead**." **GAP: no stated Amaranth livery colors** (the flower's own crimson/magenta is inferable, not written).
- **Shrine dishes / lararium visuals** — `Elyncia_02:11`: "statues of **youthful figures in lararia shrines, each clutching a rhyton (drinking horn) or patera (libation dish), dancing lightly in guardian poses**" (← direct Lares-figure render spec); `:19` "wealthiest households maintained **dedicated shrine-chambers with raised pools and sumptuous decoration**; simpler homes made do with **painted wall panels**"; `:29` "**Roman household shrine, Pompeian fresco art, fae threshold rite, orichalcum inscription** — still readable in every lararium"; `:143` "a **single inscribed orichalcum figure, a painted wall niche, or a small altar-shelf**"; `:123` offerings "food, drink, incense, first-fruits, coin"; `Elyncia_04:538` "*:tips libation dish toward the dog-headed figure on the east wall:*"; `Elyncia_04:782` "**Turn the lamps down when you leave. The node will bank its own coals.**"
- **Faerie court visual color (the governing law, deliberately non-specific)** — `Elyncia_02:23–25`: "each shrine represents a local synthesis… woven together with the **aesthetics and ceremonial traditions of native faerie heritages**… **Fae courtly aesthetics — color regimes, animal forms, procession patterns, taboo structures — interweave with Gaian shrine conventions**… producing shrines that **read as palimpsests rather than unified designs**." Courts named at `Elyncia_01:109` (Seelie / Unseelie / Ouroborous / Brimstone, ex-Summer & Winter); Brimstone = fire-aspected fae lords, dwarves, gnomes, trolls, caldera-carved (`:505–509`); insect fae clans = **hornet, beetle, dragonfly**, "pollen-based enchantments" (`:540`); Seelie = fae woods and river networks, "Faewild coast" (`:419/423`). **GAP: no per-court color assignment written anywhere.**
- **Misc high-flavor nouns for background dressing:** "**a vendor selling maps of places that do not yet exist**… buy the map of the **city with two suns and no shadows**. Coin or **true memory** accepted as payment. The vendor prefers memories." (`Elyncia_04:338, 356–360`); "**the Etheric Road… smells like ozone and unresolved arguments**" (`:336`).

