Voice active: **Lares** (Tasked Spirit register, Prism-Gleaner task-mask).

Note on paths: actual filenames are `Flying_Triremes_and_Laser_Swords_NN_*.md`, not `NN_*.md`. Line numbers below are from those files.

## 1. DELOS (all of it — thin, 4 hits corpus-wide excl. ch03)

- `/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/ftls/Flying_Triremes_and_Laser_Swords_01_Title_Introduction.md:179` — "**The Lindwyrm, Patron of New Delos**" — classed as *embodied immortal / durable avatar-being*, not distributed god: "They may rule cities, command fleets, bargain face-to-face, or appear repeatedly in the same body."
- `...01...md:216` — attribution line: "**— Hexagram Voss, Floating Librarians of Mu - High Delos Archive**". High Delos hosts a Floating Librarian archive; Voss's voice (quoted 199-214) is the tonal register of a High Delos intellectual: dry, bureaucratic-mystic ("a temporary user interface spun up when too many people query the same idea at once"; "keep your syntax loose, your metaphors polite, and your exits memorized"; "Erisian avatars: they insist they are not glitches at all, merely punchlines that arrived before the joke finished loading").
- `.../Flying_Triremes_and_Laser_Swords_10_Appendix_Null_Referee_Resources.md:489` — "**Low Delos**", scavenger-tier stratum; unearthed there: "an ancient tiger weapon—a 'soulbound lash' said to hold Rakshasa's anger". Establishes High/Low vertical class geography.
- GAP: zero architectural, street-level, or venue description of Delos anywhere in scope. No cabaret, no tavern interior, no High Delos skyline. "cabaret" = 0 hits corpus-wide.

## 2. FAERIE / COURT VOCABULARY (usable as patron factions)

