## 3. COSTUME / PROP / TECH DRESS (specification-grade)

Spirit-Talker (best single passage for a fae-spirit performer/waitstaff look):
- `...02...:122` — "noticed as **interference first: a crackle along ward-runes, frost blooming into glyphs, dust that won't settle right**. They don't float ominously—Spirits **flicker between transactions, slipping through burlesques and gossip-halls, trailing ozone and old incense**. When they manifest *Ha*, reality reacts like a device snapping back online: **hair lifts, lamps hum, cheap mirrors show the wrong angle for a heartbeat**." — *burlesques and gossip-halls* is the closest textual anchor to cabaret in the whole corpus.
- `...02...:124` — "**wardwright-shops hung with jade and doppler charms**", "Lares nodes and crossroads shrines", "sanctified thresholds"; spirits are "**fully present, slightly out of phase with the hylosphere**."
- `...02...:147` — wardwright kit: "**jade dust, wire, incense, doppler charm**"; wards heard as "**crackle, drift, harmonic clash, the tiny scream right after a glyph tastes a lie**."

Necromancer kit (d12 props, ritual-table dressing) — `...02...:74`:
- "conch (pū) · chant-scrolls (oli, mele) · **libation bowl (ʻapu, ipu)** · **salt and ʻawa** · a death-shroud with its knots · **the iron psychopomp's lantern that never rusted** · a soul-canoe wayfinding charm · **ash-tea for guest-right with the dead** · a **slametan feast-kit** · a cracked **Ainos node-key** · a **graven skull that hoards the names of the drained** · **one small bell that should not be rung here**."

Revenant body-dress — `...02...:100` "a **cadaver-knight in borrowed armor**"; `:106` "**My Bones Engraved** … a magic chisel to engrave your bones. Gain five bone inventory slots for powers on your **arms, legs, and skull**"; `:110` reflection appears "as a **pale afterimage** of the same effect." Undead maintenance visual — `...02...:102`: "a drop or two of the master's blood, some **bolts tightened**, and a fresh jolt of **magielectric juice**."

Wild Mage regalia + items (richest object table in scope) — `...02...:190, 238-249`:
- ":190 — children who **fingerpaint with sparks**, teenagers who **whistle up viridian dust-devils**, caravan guards who **juggle fire until the flames start juggling back** … turn a skirmish into a **light-show**—or a quiet campfire into a **violet crater**. Living batteries of pure chance … the nervous **counting of fire-extinguisher charms**."
- 1 **Flux-Wyld Compass** — "**Orichalcum gyroscope** that twitches toward the most 'energetic' mana node."
- 2 **Wave-Jammer Focus Lens** — "**Cracked planar-glass disk**; when held up it bends reality's currents."
- 3 **Wind-Jammer Sail Cloak** — "**Living membrane that inflates with astral wind**."
- 4 **Folded Horizon Key** — "**semiotic origami tool forged from memory-mirrors and liminal bone**."
- 5 **Entropy Harmonizer** — "**Chiming hand-bell that drinks stray Flux**."
- 6 **Wyld-Jammer Helm** — "**Crystal-studded circlet**."
- 7 **Probability Resonance Dice** — "Five **void-amber d6 whose pips flicker between 1 ↔ 6**."
- 8 **Wyldfire Strider Boots** — "**Arc-jet greaves forged from wyld-wyrm scale**."
- 9 **Holo Compass [prismatic]** — "**Crystal gyroscope that blooms a shifting holo-rose**."
- 10 **Aetheric Kite Familiar** — "**Folded planar-paper bird**."
- 12 **Chaos Mirror Circuit** — "**Obsidian-platinum wafer** … the mirror shatters until dawn."
- Named Wild Mages as patron silhouettes (`:194-199`): "**Lady Zheraphine of the Hundred-Fold Cloak**. Her **mirrored selves** maintain embassies across Elyncia's logic fractures"; "**Brother-Captain Vrax of the Æther Hussars** … keeps a campaign diary in **stellar ink that refuses to be read linearly**"; "**Doctor Δ (Delta) Kline, Flux Surgeon** … runs an **ambulatory surgical cathedral that crawls the Iron-spine mountains**"; "**Mara Morai, KSC, Battle Nun of the Edible Zen Garden**"; "**Telarus, Keeper of the Sacred Chao** … **Drinks entropy like tea**"; Amorphous Dreams Cabal (`:188`).

Grimoires as carried props (best "book" silhouettes) — `...05...:1749-1755`:
- "1. **Codex of the Sea-Filk Apocalypse** (**knotted net record, mint**) … **Plays mournful surf-guitar through any speaker within 30′** when opened."
- "2. **Heliophage Heart Glyphs** (**sun-etched memory tattoo**) … **Glows amber** when undead are within 60′."
- "3. **Lacrimae Machina Manual** (**compact phonograph**) … **nearby machines briefly weep lubricant**."
- "4. **Null Priest Litany Disk** (**artificial mnemonic lotus**) … an **ethereal chorus swells**."
- "5. **Erebus Library Tile** (**tetragonal bone-scales**)"; "6. **Quietus Memory Demi-Tome** (**pale parchment codex**)."
- `...05...:1696` — "rare '**glass-mind wafers**'" socketed "**into your cortex**."
- `...05...:1760-1770` — craft materials: "**[orichalcum] sheets**", "**stabilised [echo] crystals**", "**[dream] loop-seeds**", "**surfer-shell plates**", "**bleached [vellum]**", "**amber stasis [wax]**", "**distilled [oblivion] motes**", "**ghost-ink**", "pressed **beneath a waning moon**".

Oldtech/magitech object look — `...05...:25` — "**Ward-lamps, bottled daemons, charged staves, signal seals, shrine relays, anti-curse scarabs, and portable noosphere hacks**"; may be "**ritualized, haunted, half-alive, temple-bound, guild-licensed**". `:639` wands/staves/rods: "**conductors, command pieces, shrine handles, and oldtech emitters** … they carry hidden depletion, **ugly geometry**, or the **wrong kind of public signature**"; `:658` "**public signal bleed**". `:40` fantascience = "**buildertech, signal launchers, machine-voices, and dangerous apparatus**." Split for character-read: **magitech = Thought** (pattern-reading, occult interface, sign interpretation, `:23`); **fantascience = Charisma** (command presence, live interface, imposed will, `:38`).
Misc luminous props: `...05...:1068` **Chime of Time** — "3″ long, made of a **silvery metal** … it will **turn gold at one end, the color slowly spreading to the other end** in an hour's time"; `:1080` **Efreeti Bottle** — "large, heavy **sealed jug about 3′ high**", creature returns to "**the fabled City of Brass**"; `:1076` Displacer Cloak "**warps light rays**"; `:1152` quill "with a **nib of rare material (often orichalcum)**"; `:1123` **Lamp of Long Burning** — "metal, with a lower compartment for oil, a handle, and **shutters around the body**."

