- `...09...:200-224` — jewelry forms (wearable silhouette list for patrons): "anklet, armband, amulet, beads, belt-chain, ring, bracelet, collar, medallion, brooch, earring set, **diadem**, buckle, necklace, **crown**, cameo, pendant, **tiara**, chain, choker, **scepter**, clasp, hairpin set, **orb**, locket, **reliquary**, talisman, pin, lucky token, **scarab idol**" — top band explicitly "**Regalia** `20,000-50,000`."
- `...05...:407-410` — chromatic dragon/gem color pairs usable as court-livery keys: "White (or **Crystal**), Black (or **Onyx**), Green (or **Jade**), Blue (or **Sapphire**), Red (or **Ruby**), Gold (or **Amber**)."
- `...10...:91-119` — tag lexicon usable as flavor-adjective banks: **Elements** "[air][earth][fire][water][ice][lightning][acid][venom][smoke][steam][magma][metal][stone][sand][storm][sun][moon][star][radiant][necrotic][chromatic][gravity][heat][plasma]"; **Dreams & Shadows** "[dream][shadow][web][chaos][order][void][fear][madness][illusion][phantasm][astral][ethereal][corruption][mutation][apocrypha][wyrd][confusion]"; **Totems & Spirits** "[totem][animal][beast][plant][fungus][insect][wyrm][fae][demon][angel][undead][giant][construct][golem][vome][spirit][guardian][daemon][vampire][caller][necrobeast]"; **Schools & Traditions** "[abjuration][conjuration][divination][enchantment][evocation][illusion][necromancy][transmutation][sorcery][oldtech][fantascience][wizard][**noömagus**][**gunmaker**][**biomantic**]"; **Weird Science & Magitech** "[network][cyber][circuit][signal][pulse][resonance][overload][bio][shell][gear][**autogolem**][**wandgun**][**raygun**][plasma][portal][time][reality]".

## 7. WORLD-FRAME / ATMOSPHERE (ch01, for scene mood not costume)

- `...01...:13` — ddate stamp "**X-Day, 40th Confusion, YOLD 5491**" — corpus canon is 5491; the brief's 5492 is one year forward (flag to parent).
- `...01...:167` — daemon presence style: "a **whisper in the radio-static**, a **bad omen in a puddle**, a **helpful coincidence**, or a **haunting**"; `:161` daemons as "**coherent, sentient kaba-elementals**", "**sentient energy creature of the noosphere**", quote-source "Pseudokaula, *Why I Hunt Daemons*, **Colché acrylics**."
- `...01...:189` — "gods often do not 'show up' so much as **leak into the world through their interfaces**"; `:187` "the natural state of the gods is **absence**"; `:193` "**Immanent / Distributed / Demi-god agent**" modes.
- `...01...:203` — "her **ley-lines as nerves**, her **noosphere as breath**, her **weather as mood**, her **ruins as old memories that still have teeth**."
- `...10...:316, 341` — house tone directives: "**mythpunk, not museum**"; "**Pratchett Rule — humor and awe coexist.** Each heritage should suggest both **absurdity and meaning**"; `:342` "should fit an Ultraviolet Grasslands, Elyncia, **a tavern from the Floating Vagabond universe**, or a **floating spelljammer** without rewriting a line."

## GAPS (honest)

- **Order of Amaranth: zero hits** anywhere in the corpus (all 10 files). No iconography exists to harvest; parent must invent or source elsewhere.
- **Adventurer's Guild: zero hits** as a named body. Only generic "guilds" (`...01...:84`), "a Human 'generalist' guild advertises: 'We can do anything — for a price'" (`...10...:573`), "**Sewer Guild Oath**"/"**Guild of Shadows**" rat-folk thieves (`...10...:694-696`), "lacquer-master … rival guild" (`...10...:595`).
- **No cabaret/venue interior description** anywhere. The only adjacent lines are `...02...:122` (burlesques, gossip-halls), `...10...:551` (faerie-touched tavern), `...10...:574` (voidjammer banquet).
- **Ch08 gives no ship *appearance***, only hull stats and part names. No description of a trireme in flight, no sails/oars/wake imagery. This is the largest gap against brief item (3).
- **Ch09 is entirely tabular** — no aesthetic prose about hoards beyond `:298` referee advice ("defenders wearing **heirloom wards**, officers carrying **charged tools**, stores already **opened and rationed**").
- **Ch05 body-armor visuals are absent**; armor appears only as mechanics/tags (`[armor]`, `[harness]`). No described armor silhouette in scope.
- Chapter 06 (18k lines, Powers/ECM) was **out of scope** but contains `Faerie Bodycrafts` (`:8053`) and `Faerie Fire` (`:9282`) plus a fae-initiation note (`:595`: "**Faerie folk clans and factions often teach powers to young fae in a partially locked form**"). Likely the corpus's densest untapped fae-visual seam — recommend a follow-up pass.

Prism-Gleaner: Lares (Tasked Spirit) -> ?
